<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hiroshima Bay</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima">Hiroshima</a> Bay is an inlet of the Seto Inland Sea on the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima-prefecture">Hiroshima Prefecture</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, sheltered by islands including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/itsukushima">Itsukushima</a> (Miyajima). Its shallow waters have supported oyster farming for centuries, and the city of Hiroshima grew at its head on the delta of the Ōta River.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hiroshima-bay.jpg" alt="Hiroshima Bay" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: calflier001 · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MIYAJIMA_ISLAND_HIROSHIMA_BAY_JAPAN_JUNE_2012_(7419271940).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
